dialect protocol
protocol stdio.dwg.ac1024.snapshot
version 1
schema stdio.dwg
start file

# 🎫️26/08/10/ARTIFACT-SYSTEM-OVERHAUL-REAL-CODECS-RUNTIME-REUSE-EVOLUTION FG2: `stdio.dwg`
# (ac1024, R2004+) is BINARY-NATIVE. This file describes the PACK CONTAINER's post-unwrap
# PAYLOAD — `DwgSnapshot.bytes`, the REAL on-disk `.dwg` file verbatim (`encode_dwg` returns
# `snap.bytes.clone()`, zero further framing of its own; the SEMIO envelope itself is described
# ONCE framework-side, see ac1018's own sibling protocol file's identical note).
#
# THIS IS THE DOCUMENTED, PRE-APPROVED M2 SCOPE BOUNDARY (§6 of `📖️grammar-recipe.md`, restated
# verbatim in this FG2 brief) — ac1024's decrypt+decompress+two-level-compressed-indirection
# pipeline (LCG-XOR header decrypt with a position-dependent per-page key, a bespoke LZ77
# variant, double indirect lookup across two independently-decompressed side-tables — the REAL
# D1/D2 pipeline, `⚙️engine/🦀️component.rs`'s `locate_r2004_sections`/`decode_r2004_sections`) is
# an imperative transform pipeline, not a declarative layout description — building it into the
# protocol walker "would mean a different kind of system" (M2's own words). This is NOT a gap to
# work around; it is a correct, pre-approved scope limit.
#
# What this codec DOES read cleanly, declaratively, WITHOUT any decrypt/decompress step first —
# verified by direct read of `../🦀️component.rs`'s `dwg_version_sentinel`/
# `parse_version_header_fields` (byte-for-byte identical offsets to ac1018's own sibling facet,
# since both standards share the same plain, unencrypted AC1015+ preamble layout per LibreDWG's
# `header.spec`):
#   - the 6-byte `AC10xx` version sentinel at offset 0x00 (GENERIC across every AC10xx version —
#     not hardcoded to literally "AC1024")
#   - `maintenance_version` (RC, one byte at 0x12) and `codepage` (RS, little-endian u16 at
#     0x13-0x14)
# Byte-checked against the real `architectural.dwg` fixture (F5's own conformance fixture,
# `📚️examples/🏛️architectural/🖼️assets/📄️architectural.dwg`): offset 0x12 == 0x02
# (`maintenance_version`), offset 0x13 == 0x1E (30 decimal, ANSI_1252 codepage) — both confirmed
# by `⚙️engine/🦀️component.rs`'s own doc comments AND independently re-verified here (`xxd`).
#
# Everything past `codepage` (offset 0x15 onward) is the encrypted R2004+ file header (itself
# starting at the fixed offset 0x80, per `locate_r2004_sections`), the compressed
# section-page-map, the compressed section-info directory, and every named section's own
# encrypted+compressed pages — the full D1/D2 pipeline above, genuinely irreducible to a
# declarative field list. Modeled as ONE opaque trailing chain; the real Rust decode/encode side
# stays fully structured and independently tested (`real_fixture_d1_locates_every_named_section`/
# `real_fixture_d2_decompresses_every_section`, `⚙️engine/🦀️component.rs`).
#
# `framing record` (NOT `framing magic ...`) — same `protocol-framing-magic-fixed-8-bytes` gap
# ac1018's own sibling protocol file documents (`Framing::Magic` unconditionally reads/compares
# EXACTLY 8 raw bytes regardless of a shorter declared literal's own width; confirmed live by a
# real `walk_protocol` run against this exact 6-byte "AC1024" magic). `field magic fixed 6` is
# genuinely walked but not byte-validated at the protocol layer (the real Rust
# `dwg_version_sentinel` already validates the `AC` + 4-digit shape).
framing record
header fixed 21
field magic fixed 6
field reserved fixed 12
field maintenance_version u8
field codepage u16
chain remainder bytes
